{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0112mLH9WWwb7Sz4k4PbEBji","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nslug: pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-09\ncompleted_at:\nsupersedes:\ndepends_on:\nremediates:\npriority: 1\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\ndelivers: capability:delegate-picker-and-claude-runs\n---\n\n# Spec: The delegate picker runs in any login shell and reads at a glance\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\n\n`pose delegate watch` opens a picker whose preview works whichever login shell the user has, and whose list shows state, agent and age in columns.\n\n### Business value\n\nThe picker handed fzf a preview written as a POSIX `while` loop; fzf runs a preview with the user's login shell (`$SHELL -c`), and fish refused it (\"Missing end to balance this while loop\"), leaving the preview pane empty. The list also put the id first and cut the agent column, so a run could not be told from another. The same session found that a delegated Claude task failed on this repository: its instance policy still carried an older Claude profile whose runs end with \"the agent's output could not be redacted\", so the Claude runs showed as failed and never as work done; the profile of the engine repository ran them.\n\n### Constraints\n\n- The mechanisms are the existing ones: the fzf picker of `delegate watch`, `--refresh`, and the delegation policy of the instance.\n\n### Non-goals\n\n- Changing what `delegate watch` follows or prints.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n\n- R1: The preview command handed to fzf shall be one POSIX `sh -c '<script>' <pose> {1}` word, with the refresh loop inside the quoted script and the pose path and the run id passed as arguments, so that fish, zsh and bash all parse it.\n- R2: The list shall show the state with a one-cell glyph, the agent and the age in aligned columns and the label last, under a header, with the id hidden and still handed to the preview.\n- R3: The layout shall put the list at the top with a border, so that the preview and the list stay readable on a narrow terminal.\n\n### Non-functional\n\n- No new dependency: fzf stays the picker and the numbered menu stays the fallback.\n\n### Security\n\n- None: the script is a fixed string; the pose path and the id are arguments, never interpolated into it.\n\n### Compatibility\n\n- `delegate watch` with `--refresh 0` and the numbered menu behave as before.\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n\n`internal/cli/delegate_watch.go` and its tests.\n\n### Artifacts\n\n- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md\n- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.json\n- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md\n- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_test.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_picker_test.go\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:delegate-picker-and-claude-runs module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n\n### API/contract changes\n\nNone.\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n- [x] Reproduce the fish failure and the empty Claude runs\n- [x] Make the preview command shell-independent and test it under fish\n- [x] Lay the list out in columns with a header and a glyph\n- [x] Run a Claude task with the engine repository's profile on this repository's policy\n- [ ] Independent review and closeout\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Basis: R1\n- Minimal option: detect the login shell and write each syntax\n- Selected option: always `sh -c` with arguments\n- Rationale: one POSIX word parses in every shell, and passing the path and id as arguments keeps them out of the script\n- Consequences: the preview needs `sh`, which every system fzf runs on has\n- Falsifier: a login shell that cannot parse a single-quoted `sh -c` word\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\n\nThe preview command is run by `sh` with a fake pose and checked by `fish -n` when fish is installed; the existing picker tests keep their fake fzf.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n`go test` of `internal/cli`; the strict matrix in a clean clone.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestThePickerPreviewIsOnePOSIXWordTheLoginShellCanParse check:delegate-picker-integration\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestTheStateGlyphIsOneCellAndEveryStateHasOne test:TestThePickerRowsAlignEveryStateAndTheArgumentsHideTheID\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestDelegateWatchPicksARun test:TestThePickerRowsAlignEveryStateAndTheArgumentsHideTheID\n\n### Known gaps\n- A delegated Claude task on an instance whose policy carries the older Claude profile ends with \"the agent's output could not be redacted; it was not kept\", a message that does not name the profile. The cause inside the redaction path was not isolated; this repository's policy now carries the engine repository's profile, under which Claude tasks complete. It is a follow-up.\n- The list is not sorted or filtered by agent in the picker; `delegate ls --agent` does that.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nThe picker's preview is one `sh -c` word that fish parses (R1); the list shows glyph, state, agent and age in columns under a header with the label last and the id hidden (R2); the list sits on top with a border (R3). Left out: the diagnosis of the legacy Claude profile in the engine.\n\n### Files and modules changed\n- pose-mcp/internal/cli (delegate_watch.go, delegate_watch_test.go, delegate_watch_picker_test.go)\n- the validation matrix gains `delegate-picker-integration`\n\n### Validation executed\n- Command: `pose validate --strict --jobs 4` on a clean clone of the reviewed head\n- Result: recorded by the sealed validation evidence; independent delegated review concluded with `pose review conclude`.\n\n### Residual risks\n- The look of the picker depends on the fzf version; the numbered menu is the fallback.\n\n### Follow-ups\n\n- [open] Quote the preview command for a pose path with a backslash under a fish login shell, where single quotes still process `\\\\`; and run the fish parse check where fish is absent by failing instead of skipping in CI. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\n- [open] Name the profile in the failure of a delegated task whose agent output could not be redacted, and find why the older Claude profile produces it. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\ndiff --git a/.pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md b/.pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..231d4daa\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+---\n+spec: pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs\n+category: fixed\n+breaking: false\n+---\n+The picker of `pose delegate watch` no longer fails in fish: its preview command is one `sh -c` word that every login shell parses, and the list now shows a state glyph, the agent and the age in aligned columns under a header, with the label last.\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch.go\nindex 4a7e7369..d9937817 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch.go\n@@ -146,25 +146,14 @@ func chooseWatchedAttempt(root string, attempts []posemodel.DelegationAttempt, f\n // pickAttempt opens fzf with a live preview of the run under the cursor, or a\n // numbered menu without it.\n func pickAttempt(root string, candidates []posemodel.DelegationAttempt, f delegateFlags, stderr io.Writer) (string, error) {\n-\tlines := make([]string, 0, len(candidates))\n-\tfor _, a := range candidates {\n-\t\tlines = append(lines, fmt.Sprintf(\"%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\", a.AttemptID, a.State, a.Agent, a.Label, delegateAge(a.StartedAt)))\n-\t}\n+\tlines := pickerLines(candidates)\n \tif path, err := exec.LookPath(delegatePicker); err == nil {\n \t\tself, err := os.Executable()\n \t\tif err != nil {\n \t\t\treturn \"\", err\n \t\t}\n-\t\tpreview := shellQuote(self) + \" delegate watch {1} --no-follow --lines \" + strconv.Itoa(f.lines)\n-\t\tif f.verbose {\n-\t\t\tpreview += \" -v\"\n-\t\t}\n-\t\tif f.refresh > 0 {\n-\t\t\t// fzf replaces the preview when the cursor moves; the loop keeps\n-\t\t\t// the one in view current.\n-\t\t\tpreview = \"while :; do clear; \" + preview + \"; sleep \" + strconv.FormatFloat(f.refresh.Seconds(), 'f', -1, 64) + \"; done\"\n-\t\t}\n-\t\tcmd := exec.Command(path, \"--delimiter\", \"\\t\", \"--with-nth\", \"1..\", \"--preview\", preview, \"--preview-window\", \"right,60%\")\n+\t\tpreview := pickerPreviewCommand(self, f)\n+\t\tcmd := exec.Command(path, pickerArgs(preview, candidates)...)\n \t\tcmd.Dir = root\n \t\tcmd.Stdin = strings.NewReader(strings.Join(lines, \"\\n\") + \"\\n\")\n \t\tcmd.Stderr = stderr\n@@ -188,6 +177,81 @@ func pickAttempt(root string, candidates []posemodel.DelegationAttempt, f delega\n \treturn candidates[n-1].AttemptID, nil\n }\n \n+// pickerStateWidth is the width of the state column: the widest \"glyph state\" among the\n+// candidates, counted in code points, and never less than the header.\n+func pickerStateWidth(candidates []posemodel.DelegationAttempt) int {\n+\twidth := utf8.RuneCountInString(tr(\"STATE\", \"ESTADO\"))\n+\tfor _, a := range candidates {\n+\t\tif n := utf8.RuneCountInString(delegateStateGlyph(a.State) + \" \" + a.State); n > width {\n+\t\t\twidth = n\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\treturn width\n+}\n+\n+// pickerLines are the rows fzf shows. The id leads and is hidden (--with-nth 2..): it is what\n+// {1} hands the preview. The columns are padded so the state, the agent and the age line up\n+// and the label, which varies in length, comes last.\n+func pickerLines(candidates []posemodel.DelegationAttempt) []string {\n+\twidth := pickerStateWidth(candidates)\n+\tlines := make([]string, 0, len(candidates))\n+\tfor _, a := range candidates {\n+\t\tlines = append(lines, fmt.Sprintf(\"%s\\t%s %-18s %-5s %s\", a.AttemptID, padCells(delegateStateGlyph(a.State)+\" \"+a.State, width), a.Agent, delegateAge(a.StartedAt), a.Label))\n+\t}\n+\treturn lines\n+}\n+\n+// padCells pads to width code points; fmt pads by bytes of the rune count only for ASCII-safe\n+// widths, and the glyphs are multi-byte.\n+func padCells(s string, width int) string {\n+\tif n := utf8.RuneCountInString(s); n < width {\n+\t\treturn s + strings.Repeat(\" \", width-n)\n+\t}\n+\treturn s\n+}\n+\n+// pickerArgs are the arguments of fzf: the hidden id, the preview, the layout and the header\n+// over the same columns as the rows.\n+func pickerArgs(preview string, candidates []posemodel.DelegationAttempt) []string {\n+\treturn []string{\"--delimiter\", \"\\t\", \"--with-nth\", \"2..\", \"--preview\", preview,\n+\t\t\"--preview-window\", \"right,55%,border-left,wrap\", \"--layout\", \"reverse\", \"--height\", \"90%\", \"--border\",\n+\t\t\"--prompt\", \"run> \", \"--no-sort\",\n+\t\t\"--header\", fmt.Sprintf(\"%s %-18s %-5s %s\", padCells(tr(\"STATE\", \"ESTADO\"), pickerStateWidth(candidates)), tr(\"AGENT\", \"AGENTE\"), tr(\"AGE\", \"IDADE\"), tr(\"LABEL\", \"RÓTULO\"))}\n+}\n+\n+// pickerPreviewCommand is the command fzf runs for the run under the cursor. fzf hands it to\n+// the user's login shell ($SHELL -c), which may be fish or any other: the command is\n+// therefore one word of POSIX sh, `sh -c '<script>' <pose> {1}`, with the script in single\n+// quotes and the pose path and the id passed as arguments, never a `while` loop written in\n+// the login shell's own syntax (fish refuses it: \"Missing end to balance this while loop\").\n+func pickerPreviewCommand(self string, f delegateFlags) string {\n+\twatch := `\"$0\" delegate watch \"$1\" --no-follow --lines ` + strconv.Itoa(f.lines)\n+\tif f.verbose {\n+\t\twatch += \" -v\"\n+\t}\n+\tscript := watch\n+\tif f.refresh > 0 {\n+\t\t// fzf replaces the preview when the cursor moves; the loop keeps the one in view current.\n+\t\tscript = \"while :; do clear; \" + watch + \"; sleep \" + strconv.FormatFloat(f.refresh.Seconds(), 'f', -1, 64) + \"; done\"\n+\t}\n+\treturn \"sh -c \" + shellQuote(script) + \" \" + shellQuote(self) + \" {1}\"\n+}\n+\n+// delegateStateGlyph marks a state so a list can be read at a glance.\n+func delegateStateGlyph(state string) string {\n+\tswitch state {\n+\tcase \"running\":\n+\t\treturn \"●\"\n+\tcase \"completed\":\n+\t\treturn \"✓\"\n+\tcase \"failed\", \"stalled\":\n+\t\treturn \"✗\"\n+\tcase \"interrupted\":\n+\t\treturn \"◐\"\n+\t}\n+\treturn \"·\"\n+}\n+\n // shellQuote quotes a path for the shell fzf runs its preview with.\n func shellQuote(s string) string { return \"'\" + strings.ReplaceAll(s, \"'\", `'\\''`) + \"'\" }\n \ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_picker_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_picker_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..72832cb1\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_picker_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@\n+package cli\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"os/exec\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+\t\"time\"\n+\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n+\n+\tposemodel \"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\"\n+)\n+\n+// Spec pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.\n+\n+// R1: the preview command fzf hands to the login shell is one `sh -c` word, so it parses in\n+// fish as in any shell; the loop is inside the quoted script.\n+func TestThePickerPreviewIsOnePOSIXWordTheLoginShellCanParse(t *testing.T) {\n+\tcmd := pickerPreviewCommand(\"/home/go/.local/bin/pose\", delegateFlags{lines: 12, refresh: 2 * time.Second, verbose: true})\n+\tif !strings.HasPrefix(cmd, \"sh -c '\") || !strings.Contains(cmd, `\"$0\" delegate watch \"$1\"`) || !strings.HasSuffix(cmd, \" {1}\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the preview command is not sh -c '<script>' <pose> {1}: %s\", cmd)\n+\t}\n+\t// The loop sits inside the single quotes, so the login shell sees no `while` of its own.\n+\toutside := cmd[:strings.Index(cmd, \"'\")] + cmd[strings.LastIndex(cmd, \"'\")+1:]\n+\tif strings.Contains(outside, \"while\") || strings.Contains(outside, \"do \") || strings.Contains(outside, \"done\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a shell loop is outside the quoted script: %s\", outside)\n+\t}\n+\t// It runs: with `{1}` replaced by an id, sh executes the script (the fake pose is `echo`).\n+\trun := strings.Replace(pickerPreviewCommand(\"/bin/echo\", delegateFlags{lines: 3}), \"{1}\", \"'tat-1'\", 1)\n+\tout, err := exec.Command(\"sh\", \"-c\", run).CombinedOutput()\n+\tif err != nil || !strings.Contains(string(out), \"delegate watch tat-1 --no-follow --lines 3\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the preview did not run with the id as an argument: %q %v\", out, err)\n+\t}\n+\t// fish, when present, parses it too.\n+\tif fish, err := exec.LookPath(\"fish\"); err == nil {\n+\t\tif out, err := exec.Command(fish, \"-n\", \"-c\", pickerPreviewCommand(\"/bin/echo\", delegateFlags{lines: 3, refresh: time.Second})).CombinedOutput(); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"fish refuses the preview command: %s\", out)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// R2: a list line carries the state, the agent and the age in columns, the label last.\n+func TestTheStateGlyphIsOneCellAndEveryStateHasOne(t *testing.T) {\n+\tfor _, state := range []string{\"running\", \"completed\", \"failed\", \"stalled\", \"interrupted\", \"other\"} {\n+\t\tif len([]rune(delegateStateGlyph(state))) != 1 {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"state %s has no one-cell glyph\", state)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// R2/R3: the rows and the arguments of the picker. The state column is as wide as the widest\n+// \"glyph state\" in code points, so no state shifts the columns after it; the id leads and is\n+// hidden; the layout is reversed with a border and a header over the same columns.\n+func TestThePickerRowsAlignEveryStateAndTheArgumentsHideTheID(t *testing.T) {\n+\tcandidates := []posemodel.DelegationAttempt{\n+\t\t{AttemptID: \"a1\", State: \"completed\", Agent: \"x\", Label: \"one\"},\n+\t\t{AttemptID: \"a2\", State: \"interrupted\", Agent: \"y\", Label: \"two\"},\n+\t\t{AttemptID: \"a3\", State: \"running\", Agent: \"z\", Label: \"three\"},\n+\t}\n+\tvar agentAt []int\n+\tfor i, line := range pickerLines(candidates) {\n+\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(line, candidates[i].AttemptID+\"\\t\") {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"the id does not lead row %d: %q\", i, line)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\t_, rest, _ := strings.Cut(line, \"\\t\")\n+\t\tat := utf8.RuneCountInString(rest[:strings.Index(rest, string(candidates[i].Agent[0])+\" \")])\n+\t\tagentAt = append(agentAt, at)\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, at := range agentAt {\n+\t\tif at != agentAt[0] {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the agent column shifts between states: %v\", agentAt)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tif want := utf8.RuneCountInString(\"◐ interrupted\"); agentAt[0] < want {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"the state column (%d) is narrower than the widest state (%d)\", agentAt[0], want)\n+\t}\n+\targs := strings.Join(pickerArgs(\"PREVIEW\", candidates), \"\\x00\")\n+\tfor _, want := range []string{\"--with-nth\\x002..\", \"--layout\\x00reverse\", \"--border\", \"--preview\\x00PREVIEW\", \"--delimiter\\x00\\t\"} {\n+\t\tif !strings.Contains(args, want) {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"the picker arguments lack %q\", want)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\theader := pickerArgs(\"P\", candidates)\n+\thdr := header[len(header)-1]\n+\tif got := utf8.RuneCountInString(hdr[:strings.Index(hdr, \"AGENT\")]); got != agentAt[0] {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"the header does not line up with the rows: %q\", hdr)\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_test.go\nindex e670513e..f0ce651c 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_test.go\n@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@ func TestDelegateWatchPicksARun(t *testing.T) {\n \tdelegatePicker = fake\n \tcode, out, errOut = runPoseSplit(t, root, \"delegate\", \"watch\", \"--no-follow\", \"--refresh\", \"0\")\n \trecorded, _ := os.ReadFile(argsFile)\n-\tif code != 0 || !strings.Contains(string(recorded), \"delegate watch {1} --no-follow\") || strings.Contains(string(recorded), \"while :\") || !strings.Contains(out, \"■ completed\") {\n+\tif code != 0 || !strings.Contains(string(recorded), `delegate watch \"$1\" --no-follow`) || strings.Contains(string(recorded), \"while :\") || !strings.Contains(out, \"■ completed\") {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"fzf: %d %s %s args=%s\", code, out, errOut, recorded)\n \t}\n \trunPoseSplit(t, root, \"delegate\", \"watch\", \"--no-follow\")","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"a08e8d0d-e75e-454a-bd5a-d137510ec874","timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:51:28.583Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"---\nslug: pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-09\ncompleted_at:\nsupersedes:\ndepends_on:\nremediates:\npriority: 1\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\ndelivers: capability:delegate-picker-and-claude-runs\n---\n\n# Spec: The delegate picker runs in any login shell and reads at a glance\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\n\n`pose delegate watch` opens a picker whose preview works whichever login shell the user has, and whose list shows state, agent and age in columns.\n\n### Business value\n\nThe picker handed fzf a preview written as a POSIX `while` loop; fzf runs a preview with the user's login shell (`$SHELL -c`), and fish refused it (\"Missing end to balance this while loop\"), leaving the preview pane empty. The list also put the id first and cut the agent column, so a run could not be told from another. The same session found that a delegated Claude task failed on this repository: its instance policy still carried an older Claude profile whose runs end with \"the agent's output could not be redacted\", so the Claude runs showed as failed and never as work done; the profile of the engine repository ran them.\n\n### Constraints\n\n- The mechanisms are the existing ones: the fzf picker of `delegate watch`, `--refresh`, and the delegation policy of the instance.\n\n### Non-goals\n\n- Changing what `delegate watch` follows or prints.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n\n- R1: The preview command handed to fzf shall be one POSIX `sh -c '<script>' <pose> {1}` word, with the refresh loop inside the quoted script and the pose path and the run id passed as arguments, so that fish, zsh and bash all parse it.\n- R2: The list shall show the state with a one-cell glyph, the agent and the age in aligned columns and the label last, under a header, with the id hidden and still handed to the preview.\n- R3: The layout shall put the list at the top with a border, so that the preview and the list stay readable on a narrow terminal.\n\n### Non-functional\n\n- No new dependency: fzf stays the picker and the numbered menu stays the fallback.\n\n### Security\n\n- None: the script is a fixed string; the pose path and the id are arguments, never interpolated into it.\n\n### Compatibility\n\n- `delegate watch` with `--refresh 0` and the numbered menu behave as before.\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n\n`internal/cli/delegate_watch.go` and its tests.\n\n### Artifacts\n\n- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md\n- created: .pose/starts/pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.json\n- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md\n- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_test.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_picker_test.go\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:delegate-picker-and-claude-runs module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n\n### API/contract changes\n\nNone.\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n- [x] Reproduce the fish failure and the empty Claude runs\n- [x] Make the preview command shell-independent and test it under fish\n- [x] Lay the list out in columns with a header and a glyph\n- [x] Run a Claude task with the engine repository's profile on this repository's policy\n- [ ] Independent review and closeout\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Basis: R1\n- Minimal option: detect the login shell and write each syntax\n- Selected option: always `sh -c` with arguments\n- Rationale: one POSIX word parses in every shell, and passing the path and id as arguments keeps them out of the script\n- Consequences: the preview needs `sh`, which every system fzf runs on has\n- Falsifier: a login shell that cannot parse a single-quoted `sh -c` word\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\n\nThe preview command is run by `sh` with a fake pose and checked by `fish -n` when fish is installed; the existing picker tests keep their fake fzf.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n`go test` of `internal/cli`; the strict matrix in a clean clone.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestThePickerPreviewIsOnePOSIXWordTheLoginShellCanParse check:delegate-picker-integration\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestTheStateGlyphIsOneCellAndEveryStateHasOne test:TestThePickerRowsAlignEveryStateAndTheArgumentsHideTheID\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestDelegateWatchPicksARun test:TestThePickerRowsAlignEveryStateAndTheArgumentsHideTheID\n\n### Known gaps\n- A delegated Claude task on an instance whose policy carries the older Claude profile ends with \"the agent's output could not be redacted; it was not kept\", a message that does not name the profile. The cause inside the redaction path was not isolated; this repository's policy now carries the engine repository's profile, under which Claude tasks complete. It is a follow-up.\n- The list is not sorted or filtered by agent in the picker; `delegate ls --agent` does that.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nThe picker's preview is one `sh -c` word that fish parses (R1); the list shows glyph, state, agent and age in columns under a header with the label last and the id hidden (R2); the list sits on top with a border (R3). Left out: the diagnosis of the legacy Claude profile in the engine.\n\n### Files and modules changed\n- pose-mcp/internal/cli (delegate_watch.go, delegate_watch_test.go, delegate_watch_picker_test.go)\n- the validation matrix gains `delegate-picker-integration`\n\n### Validation executed\n- Command: `pose validate --strict --jobs 4` on a clean clone of the reviewed head\n- Result: recorded by the sealed validation evidence; independent delegated review concluded with `pose review conclude`.\n\n### Residual risks\n- The look of the picker depends on the fzf version; the numbered menu is the fallback.\n\n### Follow-ups\n\n- [open] Quote the preview command for a pose path with a backslash under a fish login shell, where single quotes still process `\\\\`; and run the fish parse check where fish is absent by failing instead of skipping in CI. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\n- [open] Name the profile in the failure of a delegated task whose agent output could not be redacted, and find why the older Claude profile produces it. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\ndiff --git a/.pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md b/.pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..231d4daa\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+---\n+spec: pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs\n+category: fixed\n+breaking: false\n+---\n+The picker of `pose delegate watch` no longer fails in fish: its preview command is one `sh -c` word that every login shell parses, and the list now shows a state glyph, the agent and the age in aligned columns under a header, with the label last.\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch.go\nindex 4a7e7369..d9937817 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch.go\n@@ -146,25 +146,14 @@ func chooseWatchedAttempt(root string, attempts []posemodel.DelegationAttempt, f\n // pickAttempt opens fzf with a live preview of the run under the cursor, or a\n // numbered menu without it.\n func pickAttempt(root string, candidates []posemodel.DelegationAttempt, f delegateFlags, stderr io.Writer) (string, error) {\n-\tlines := make([]string, 0, len(candidates))\n-\tfor _, a := range candidates {\n-\t\tlines = append(lines, fmt.Sprintf(\"%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\", a.AttemptID, a.State, a.Agent, a.Label, delegateAge(a.StartedAt)))\n-\t}\n+\tlines := pickerLines(candidates)\n \tif path, err := exec.LookPath(delegatePicker); err == nil {\n \t\tself, err := os.Executable()\n \t\tif err != nil {\n \t\t\treturn \"\", err\n \t\t}\n-\t\tpreview := shellQuote(self) + \" delegate watch {1} --no-follow --lines \" + strconv.Itoa(f.lines)\n-\t\tif f.verbose {\n-\t\t\tpreview += \" -v\"\n-\t\t}\n-\t\tif f.refresh > 0 {\n-\t\t\t// fzf replaces the preview when the cursor moves; the loop keeps\n-\t\t\t// the one in view current.\n-\t\t\tpreview = \"while :; do clear; \" + preview + \"; sleep \" + strconv.FormatFloat(f.refresh.Seconds(), 'f', -1, 64) + \"; done\"\n-\t\t}\n-\t\tcmd := exec.Command(path, \"--delimiter\", \"\\t\", \"--with-nth\", \"1..\", \"--preview\", preview, \"--preview-window\", \"right,60%\")\n+\t\tpreview := pickerPreviewCommand(self, f)\n+\t\tcmd := exec.Command(path, pickerArgs(preview, candidates)...)\n \t\tcmd.Dir = root\n \t\tcmd.Stdin = strings.NewReader(strings.Join(lines, \"\\n\") + \"\\n\")\n \t\tcmd.Stderr = stderr\n@@ -188,6 +177,81 @@ func pickAttempt(root string, candidates []posemodel.DelegationAttempt, f delega\n \treturn candidates[n-1].AttemptID, nil\n }\n \n+// pickerStateWidth is the width of the state column: the widest \"glyph state\" among the\n+// candidates, counted in code points, and never less than the header.\n+func pickerStateWidth(candidates []posemodel.DelegationAttempt) int {\n+\twidth := utf8.RuneCountInString(tr(\"STATE\", \"ESTADO\"))\n+\tfor _, a := range candidates {\n+\t\tif n := utf8.RuneCountInString(delegateStateGlyph(a.State) + \" \" + a.State); n > width {\n+\t\t\twidth = n\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\treturn width\n+}\n+\n+// pickerLines are the rows fzf shows. The id leads and is hidden (--with-nth 2..): it is what\n+// {1} hands the preview. The columns are padded so the state, the agent and the age line up\n+// and the label, which varies in length, comes last.\n+func pickerLines(candidates []posemodel.DelegationAttempt) []string {\n+\twidth := pickerStateWidth(candidates)\n+\tlines := make([]string, 0, len(candidates))\n+\tfor _, a := range candidates {\n+\t\tlines = append(lines, fmt.Sprintf(\"%s\\t%s %-18s %-5s %s\", a.AttemptID, padCells(delegateStateGlyph(a.State)+\" \"+a.State, width), a.Agent, delegateAge(a.StartedAt), a.Label))\n+\t}\n+\treturn lines\n+}\n+\n+// padCells pads to width code points; fmt pads by bytes of the rune count only for ASCII-safe\n+// widths, and the glyphs are multi-byte.\n+func padCells(s string, width int) string {\n+\tif n := utf8.RuneCountInString(s); n < width {\n+\t\treturn s + strings.Repeat(\" \", width-n)\n+\t}\n+\treturn s\n+}\n+\n+// pickerArgs are the arguments of fzf: the hidden id, the preview, the layout and the header\n+// over the same columns as the rows.\n+func pickerArgs(preview string, candidates []posemodel.DelegationAttempt) []string {\n+\treturn []string{\"--delimiter\", \"\\t\", \"--with-nth\", \"2..\", \"--preview\", preview,\n+\t\t\"--preview-window\", \"right,55%,border-left,wrap\", \"--layout\", \"reverse\", \"--height\", \"90%\", \"--border\",\n+\t\t\"--prompt\", \"run> \", \"--no-sort\",\n+\t\t\"--header\", fmt.Sprintf(\"%s %-18s %-5s %s\", padCells(tr(\"STATE\", \"ESTADO\"), pickerStateWidth(candidates)), tr(\"AGENT\", \"AGENTE\"), tr(\"AGE\", \"IDADE\"), tr(\"LABEL\", \"RÓTULO\"))}\n+}\n+\n+// pickerPreviewCommand is the command fzf runs for the run under the cursor. fzf hands it to\n+// the user's login shell ($SHELL -c), which may be fish or any other: the command is\n+// therefore one word of POSIX sh, `sh -c '<script>' <pose> {1}`, with the script in single\n+// quotes and the pose path and the id passed as arguments, never a `while` loop written in\n+// the login shell's own syntax (fish refuses it: \"Missing end to balance this while loop\").\n+func pickerPreviewCommand(self string, f delegateFlags) string {\n+\twatch := `\"$0\" delegate watch \"$1\" --no-follow --lines ` + strconv.Itoa(f.lines)\n+\tif f.verbose {\n+\t\twatch += \" -v\"\n+\t}\n+\tscript := watch\n+\tif f.refresh > 0 {\n+\t\t// fzf replaces the preview when the cursor moves; the loop keeps the one in view current.\n+\t\tscript = \"while :; do clear; \" + watch + \"; sleep \" + strconv.FormatFloat(f.refresh.Seconds(), 'f', -1, 64) + \"; done\"\n+\t}\n+\treturn \"sh -c \" + shellQuote(script) + \" \" + shellQuote(self) + \" {1}\"\n+}\n+\n+// delegateStateGlyph marks a state so a list can be read at a glance.\n+func delegateStateGlyph(state string) string {\n+\tswitch state {\n+\tcase \"running\":\n+\t\treturn \"●\"\n+\tcase \"completed\":\n+\t\treturn \"✓\"\n+\tcase \"failed\", \"stalled\":\n+\t\treturn \"✗\"\n+\tcase \"interrupted\":\n+\t\treturn \"◐\"\n+\t}\n+\treturn \"·\"\n+}\n+\n // shellQuote quotes a path for the shell fzf runs its preview with.\n func shellQuote(s string) string { return \"'\" + strings.ReplaceAll(s, \"'\", `'\\''`) + \"'\" }\n \ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_picker_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_picker_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..72832cb1\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_picker_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@\n+package cli\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"os/exec\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+\t\"time\"\n+\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n+\n+\tposemodel \"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\"\n+)\n+\n+// Spec pose-delegate-picker-and-claude-runs.\n+\n+// R1: the preview command fzf hands to the login shell is one `sh -c` word, so it parses in\n+// fish as in any shell; the loop is inside the quoted script.\n+func TestThePickerPreviewIsOnePOSIXWordTheLoginShellCanParse(t *testing.T) {\n+\tcmd := pickerPreviewCommand(\"/home/go/.local/bin/pose\", delegateFlags{lines: 12, refresh: 2 * time.Second, verbose: true})\n+\tif !strings.HasPrefix(cmd, \"sh -c '\") || !strings.Contains(cmd, `\"$0\" delegate watch \"$1\"`) || !strings.HasSuffix(cmd, \" {1}\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the preview command is not sh -c '<script>' <pose> {1}: %s\", cmd)\n+\t}\n+\t// The loop sits inside the single quotes, so the login shell sees no `while` of its own.\n+\toutside := cmd[:strings.Index(cmd, \"'\")] + cmd[strings.LastIndex(cmd, \"'\")+1:]\n+\tif strings.Contains(outside, \"while\") || strings.Contains(outside, \"do \") || strings.Contains(outside, \"done\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a shell loop is outside the quoted script: %s\", outside)\n+\t}\n+\t// It runs: with `{1}` replaced by an id, sh executes the script (the fake pose is `echo`).\n+\trun := strings.Replace(pickerPreviewCommand(\"/bin/echo\", delegateFlags{lines: 3}), \"{1}\", \"'tat-1'\", 1)\n+\tout, err := exec.Command(\"sh\", \"-c\", run).CombinedOutput()\n+\tif err != nil || !strings.Contains(string(out), \"delegate watch tat-1 --no-follow --lines 3\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the preview did not run with the id as an argument: %q %v\", out, err)\n+\t}\n+\t// fish, when present, parses it too.\n+\tif fish, err := exec.LookPath(\"fish\"); err == nil {\n+\t\tif out, err := exec.Command(fish, \"-n\", \"-c\", pickerPreviewCommand(\"/bin/echo\", delegateFlags{lines: 3, refresh: time.Second})).CombinedOutput(); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"fish refuses the preview command: %s\", out)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// R2: a list line carries the state, the agent and the age in columns, the label last.\n+func TestTheStateGlyphIsOneCellAndEveryStateHasOne(t *testing.T) {\n+\tfor _, state := range []string{\"running\", \"completed\", \"failed\", \"stalled\", \"interrupted\", \"other\"} {\n+\t\tif len([]rune(delegateStateGlyph(state))) != 1 {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"state %s has no one-cell glyph\", state)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// R2/R3: the rows and the arguments of the picker. The state column is as wide as the widest\n+// \"glyph state\" in code points, so no state shifts the columns after it; the id leads and is\n+// hidden; the layout is reversed with a border and a header over the same columns.\n+func TestThePickerRowsAlignEveryStateAndTheArgumentsHideTheID(t *testing.T) {\n+\tcandidates := []posemodel.DelegationAttempt{\n+\t\t{AttemptID: \"a1\", State: \"completed\", Agent: \"x\", Label: \"one\"},\n+\t\t{AttemptID: \"a2\", State: \"interrupted\", Agent: \"y\", Label: \"two\"},\n+\t\t{AttemptID: \"a3\", State: \"running\", Agent: \"z\", Label: \"three\"},\n+\t}\n+\tvar agentAt []int\n+\tfor i, line := range pickerLines(candidates) {\n+\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(line, candidates[i].AttemptID+\"\\t\") {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"the id does not lead row %d: %q\", i, line)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\t_, rest, _ := strings.Cut(line, \"\\t\")\n+\t\tat := utf8.RuneCountInString(rest[:strings.Index(rest, string(candidates[i].Agent[0])+\" \")])\n+\t\tagentAt = append(agentAt, at)\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, at := range agentAt {\n+\t\tif at != agentAt[0] {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the agent column shifts between states: %v\", agentAt)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tif want := utf8.RuneCountInString(\"◐ interrupted\"); agentAt[0] < want {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"the state column (%d) is narrower than the widest state (%d)\", agentAt[0], want)\n+\t}\n+\targs := strings.Join(pickerArgs(\"PREVIEW\", candidates), \"\\x00\")\n+\tfor _, want := range []string{\"--with-nth\\x002..\", \"--layout\\x00reverse\", \"--border\", \"--preview\\x00PREVIEW\", \"--delimiter\\x00\\t\"} {\n+\t\tif !strings.Contains(args, want) {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"the picker arguments lack %q\", want)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\theader := pickerArgs(\"P\", candidates)\n+\thdr := header[len(header)-1]\n+\tif got := utf8.RuneCountInString(hdr[:strings.Index(hdr, \"AGENT\")]); got != agentAt[0] {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"the header does not line up with the rows: %q\", hdr)\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_test.go\nindex e670513e..f0ce651c 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_watch_test.go\n@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@ func TestDelegateWatchPicksARun(t *testing.T) {\n \tdelegatePicker = fake\n \tcode, out, errOut = runPoseSplit(t, root, \"delegate\", \"watch\", \"--no-follow\", \"--refresh\", \"0\")\n \trecorded, _ := os.ReadFile(argsFile)\n-\tif code != 0 || !strings.Contains(string(recorded), \"delegate watch {1} --no-follow\") || strings.Contains(string(recorded), \"while :\") || !strings.Contains(out, \"■ completed\") {\n+\tif code != 0 || !strings.Contains(string(recorded), `delegate watch \"$1\" --no-follow`) || strings.Contains(string(recorded), \"while :\") || !strings.Contains(out, \"■ completed\") {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"fzf: %d %s %s args=%s\", code, out, errOut, recorded)\n \t}\n \trunPoseSplit(t, root, \"delegate\", \"watch\", \"--no-follow\")","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0112mLH9WWwb7Sz4k4PbEBji","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
